        "text": "Thank you, Sofia. My key message today is simple: trust is a contract that nobody signs. Let me give you one case. Two years ago, my club was negotiating a renewal with a big sponsor. The sponsor said that they wanted a longer contract, and we wanted a higher fee. We found a compromise, and the vote was unanimous. But what really closed the deal was not the money. It was our track record. The sponsor told us that they had checked every audit from the last five years. The reason why they trusted us is that we had always published the results, the good ones and the bad ones. So my takeaway for you is this: if you want partners to trust you tomorrow, be transparent today. Thank you."
